## C. The reading (direct)

Every instrument built on 2026-09-02 — the cusp/homology cage, the
source curve E, the boundary package at general N, the meridian
floor, the polar ledger, the pencil genus, the satellite mass, the
Puiseux depth, and now the contact deficiency on Moh's tree — bounds
in one direction: D (or n, T, Ψ) from BELOW in N, or N from ABOVE
in D. A ceiling D ≤ C(N), the one statement that would cross Moh's
floor and finish the H2 residual, needs N bounded from BELOW by D.
No instrument in the record supplies that, and this lane shows why
the boundary tree cannot: its free datum (the sub-tree of D_1) only
ever lowers N. The campaign-level question is therefore
**OPEN[UPPER-TO-FLOOR]** (bounded: the integer N ∈ [2, 16] at a
degree-minimal counterexample): name a mechanism that bounds N below
by D, or prove that none exists on the boundary and redirect.

What the instrument CAN do is also new and concrete: it attaches an
N-window to every Moh skeleton, and pins 418 skeletons at
D ∈ [101, 200] to N = 4 exactly. Those are the first concrete
realisation targets the counterexample side has ever had — a
degree-minimal counterexample with N = 4 at an admissible degree must
have one of a finite, listed set of skeletons, each with U = 4.

