+## Strongest Counterexample Attack
+
+Try to realize the same `D=105,N=4` skeleton, deliberately using proportional
+bottom structure to keep the contact deficiency small. The construction should
+not start from full coefficient boxes of degrees `42` and `105`. Start from the
+approximate-root/Puiseux data of the skeleton, solve the bottom `[f,g]=1`
+equations, then ask row 4/31 whether the local object algebraizes and whether
+row 32's collision ideal produces an off-diagonal point.
